        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users resolving exec-backed SecretRefs could get inherited Object prototype members treated as provider response entries when the requested id matched names such as `toString`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nExec provider responses now check `values` and `errors` with own-property membership before accepting an id. The change is scoped to exec response parsing and keeps the existing missing-id and per-id error behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators get deterministic SecretRef failures when an exec provider omits a requested id, including ids that collide with Object prototype names, instead of accidentally reading inherited values.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\nBehavior addressed: an exec SecretRef provider can omit a requested id named `toString`; the resolver must treat that as a missing provider response entry, not as an inherited Object prototype member.\n\nEnvironment: local checkout of this PR branch `alix/secrets-exec-own-ids`, Node.js via the repository `tsx` loader. The provider was a real executable shell script created in a private temp directory with mode `0700`; it read stdin and returned the real exec-provider protocol payload `{\"protocolVersion\":1,\"values\":{}}` on stdout.\n\nCommand run after this patch:\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx --input-type=module <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { resolveSecretRefString } from \"./src/secrets/resolve.ts\";\n\nconst root = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"openclaw-exec-secretref-proof-\"));\nawait fs.chmod(root, 0o700);\nconst provider = path.join(root, \"missing-toString-provider.sh\");\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  provider,\n  [\n    \"#!/bin/sh\",\n    \"cat >/dev/null\",\n    \"printf '%s' '{\\\"protocolVersion\\\":1,\\\"values\\\":{}}'\",\n  ].join(\"\\n\"),\n  { mode: 0o700 },\n);\nawait fs.chmod(provider, 0o700);\n\nconst config = {\n  secrets: {\n    providers: {\n      liveexec: {\n        source: \"exec\",\n        command: provider,\n        passEnv: [\"PATH\"],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nconst ref = { source: \"exec\", provider: \"liveexec\", id: \"toString\" };\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  proof: \"exec SecretRef provider missing inherited id\",\n  providerScript: provider.replace(root, \"<tmp-proof-dir>\"),\n  providerOutput: { protocolVersion: 1, values: {} },\n  requestedRef: ref,\n}, null, 2));\n\ntry {\n  await resolveSecretRefString(ref, { config, env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"\" } });\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({ result: \"unexpected-success\" }, null, 2));\n  process.exitCode = 1;\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({\n    result: \"expected-failure\",\n    errorName: error?.name,\n    errorMessage: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n  }, null, 2));\n  if (!(error instanceof Error) || !error.message.includes('response missing id \"toString\"')) {\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n  }\n}\n\nawait fs.rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\nEOF\n```\n\nObserved output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"proof\": \"exec SecretRef provider missing inherited id\",\n  \"providerScript\": \"<tmp-proof-dir>/missing-toString-provider.sh\",\n  \"providerOutput\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": 1,\n    \"values\": {}\n  },\n  \"requestedRef\": {\n    \"source\": \"exec\",\n    \"provider\": \"liveexec\",\n    \"id\": \"toString\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"result\": \"expected-failure\",\n  \"errorName\": \"SecretRefResolutionError\",\n  \"errorMessage\": \"Exec provider \\\"liveexec\\\" response missing id \\\"toString\\\".\"\n}\n```\n\nThis exercises the real exec-provider path without mocking `spawn`: OpenClaw starts the configured provider command, sends the protocol request over stdin, parses stdout, then resolves the requested `exec:liveexec:toString` SecretRef. After the patch, the missing `toString` id fails deterministically as a missing response id.\n\nWhat was not tested: no external secret manager or private credential store was contacted; the provider script returned only an empty protocol response and no secret material.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/secrets/resolve.test.ts` (27 tests passed)\n- Live exec SecretRef proof above: real executable provider returning an empty response for requested id `toString` now fails with `Exec provider \"liveexec\" response missing id \"toString\".`\n- Pre-PR collision check: no open PRs touched `src/secrets/resolve.ts` or `src/secrets/resolve.test.ts`; no open PR covered exec response id inherited-key handling.\n\n## CI Note\n\nThe only observed CI failure at the time of this update was `checks-node-compact-small-whole-2`, timing out in `src/tui/tui-pty-local.e2e.test.ts > creates and adopts a fresh session through the real Gateway backend`. That shard does not touch `src/secrets/resolve.ts` or `src/secrets/resolve.test.ts`; the focused secrets test and the full secrets project test passed locally.\n",
